 "notes": [
  [
   "SAO++ power select: the switch common feeds the board. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell (through D13).",
   [
    25.4,
    30.48
   ]
  ],
  [
   "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other.",
   [
    25.4,
    34.29
   ]
  ],
  [
   "D13 (series Schottky, docs/standard.md section 3) is required: the ATtiny's PB1 is wired to SAO GPIO2 through R5, so the badge could push current into the cell through the chip.",
   [
    25.4,
    38.1
   ]
  ],
  [
   "R5 (330 ohm) is the SAO spec's series resistor on a GPIO the add-on may drive. PB1 is the maker's button pin; the chip has no other spare pin (PB0, PB2, PB3, PB4 drive the LEDs, PB5 is reset).",
   [
    25.4,
    41.91
   ]
  ],
  [
   "Maker's circuit (davedarko, Eagle 2017, REV1): ATtiny85 charlieplexes 12 LEDs from PB0, PB2, PB3, PB4, each through its own resistor to one node (maker's nets N$9, N$11, N$12, N$2 = NODE_A..D).",
   [
    154.94,
    30.48
   ]
  ],
  [
   "Resistors 330 ohm (maker: 150 ohm); a lit LED sees two in series: about 2.3 mA at 3.3 V, about 1.4 mA on the cell after D13. D1..D12 are on the FRONT where the maker had LED1..LED12.",
   [
    154.94,
    34.29
   ]
  ],
  [
   "JP1: the maker's six AVR ISP pads (bare copper). SW2: the maker's push button on PB1 (pressed = low).",
   [
    101.6,
    154.94
   ]
  ]
 ]
}